# Design: Agent-pane liveness check before attach

## Problem
Nightly run 41027528544 (and the three nights before it) hung
an_agent_that_exits_at_once_leaves_nothing_behind on macos-15 only.

## Root cause
compose_outside splits a margin pane into the agent window before
attaching. If that split lands before /bin/false exits, the margin
pane keeps the session alive after the agent pane closes. The old
session_exists check then passed, attach() (which has no timeout)
blocked forever, and wait_exit(20s) returned None. Linux runners
always lost the race the other way: the agent pane was already gone
when split-window arrived, so the desk_or_agent_failure path fired.

## Approach
Record the agent pane id from new-session/new-window -P -F
'#{window_id} #{pane_id}' and refuse to attach once that pane is
missing from list-panes -a. Verified on a private socket that the
macos state is detectable: session survives, pane list does not.

## Gotchas
- An agent that dies after the liveness check still leaves the desk
  attached to the surviving margin pane; that is a normal desk losing
  its agent, not a composition failure.
- agent_pane_closed treats an empty captured id as alive, so an
  unexpected -P report degrades to the old session/window checks.
